      "text": "I've marked the run as anomalous: during growth, tube pressure has climbed steadily from 3.04 to 3.33 Torr even though argon flow has held at about 100 sccm. Temperature control looks normal (750 °C, heater power about 46%), and there's no characterization of the sample yet.\n\nThe fault is in the instrument or process, but I can't say which one. The pressure rise fits either a partly blocked exhaust or a seal leak letting air in. Without the exhaust O2 sensor, which isn't installed, the atmosphere can't be checked. That also means a sample grown under these conditions may not count as a fair test of the recipe.\n\nI've proposed a test to tell the two apart: a leak-rate check with the tube sealed, an inspection of the pump, exhaust line and valves, or a portable O2 or leak detector at the exhaust."
